  "nl_text": "The rschema_0444 database is designed to manage student information and their interactions with courses and instructors. The Student table stores details about each student, including their age, game preference, gender, name, phone number, and a unique student ID, which serves as the primary key. The Instructor table contains information about each instructor, such as their gender, name, title, and work duration, with the instructor ID being the primary key. The Course table holds details about each course, including its name, credits, location, and the instructor ID, which references the Instructor table and is not nullable. The Attendance_Record table tracks student attendance, with columns for attendance status, check-in and class times, remarks, and foreign keys referencing the Course and Student tables, with a composite primary key consisting of student ID, course ID, and check-in time. The Leave_Record table similarly tracks student leaves, with columns for class time, leave reason, status, leave time, and foreign keys referencing the Course and Student tables, with a composite primary key consisting of student ID, course ID, and leave time.",
  "gold_question": "The system is a student attendance management system. In student management, the system maintains basic information for each student, including Student ID, name, age, phone number, game preference, and gender. In course management, the system records detailed information for each course, including Course ID, course name, location, credits, and instructor ID. In instructor management, the system maintains basic information for instructors, including Instructor ID, name, gender, title, and work duration. In attendance management, the system automatically records student attendance check-ins, including Student ID, Course ID, check-in time, attendance status, class time, and remarks, achieving automated attendance management. In leave management, the system tracks and records student leave requests, including Student ID, Course ID, leave time, class time, leave reason, and leave status, facilitating comprehensive management of student attendance by the school. The system achieves automated recording of student attendance, standardized management of leave requests, and unified maintenance of course and instructor information through the collaborative functioning of these functional modules.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_llama31/0444.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0444\nCREATE TABLE `student` (\n  `student_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `age` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `gender` char(1) NOT NULL,\n  `game_preference` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `phone_number` varchar(15) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`student_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `instructor` (\n  `instructor_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `gender` char(1) NOT NULL,\n  `title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `work_duration` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`instructor_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `course` (\n  `course_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `credits` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `location` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `instructor_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`course_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `course_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`instructor_id`) REFERENCES `instructor` (`instructor_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `attendance_record` (\n  `student_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `course_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `check_in_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `attendance_status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `class_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `remarks` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`student_id`, `course_id`, `check_in_time`),\n  CONSTRAINT `attendance_record_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`student_id`) REFERENCES `student` (`student_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `attendance_record_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`course_id`) REFERENCES `course` (`course_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `leave_record` (\n  `student_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `course_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `leave_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `class_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `leave_reason` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`student_id`, `course_id`, `leave_time`),\n  CONSTRAINT `leave_record_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`student_id`) REFERENCES `student` (`student_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `leave_record_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`course_id`) REFERENCES `course` (`course_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
